{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2\cf2{\f1 .SYNOPSIS Convert a PowerShell-style wildcard pattern to an anchored, case-insensitive regex that matches the pattern ANYWHERE in the target (substring-by-default). .DESCRIPTION '*' becomes '.*' (any run of chars) and '?' becomes '.' (a single char); every other character is regex-escaped. The result is wrapped with '.*' on both sides so a bare substring (e.g. 'PROD') still matches, while explicit wildcards (e.g. 'PROD-*', 'srv-0?') are honoured.\f0}\par}
